Step 1: Textual String Deconstruction
The first step in this process is to deconstruct the string into individual elements. We will use the PHP explode function to separate the string into words. Before that, it's necessary to remove any punctuation and convert all characters to lower case for accuracy.

Step 2: Word Separation
Once we convert the string into an array of words, we can proceed to the next step. We will create a new array with unique words only.

Step 3: Unique Word Identification
PHP provides an array_unique function that removes duplicates from an array. We will use this function to get an array with unique words only.

Step 4: Count Calculation
Finally, we will use the count function to get the total number of unique words in the array.

